% Generate `tools/base_tool.py`: the abstract `BaseTool` every OpenNolan tool
% inherits, plus the enums/dataclasses of its expanded ToolContract. It enforces a
% uniform interface for discovery, execution, cost estimation, and health reporting.
% Use `from __future__ import annotations`. Import: hashlib, inspect, json, os,
% platform, subprocess, shutil, abc(ABC, abstractmethod), dataclasses(dataclass, field),
% enum(Enum), pathlib(Path), typing(Any, Callable, Optional).

## `_load_dotenv()` — run once at import (call it at module top level after defining it)

Load a BYOK `.env` into `os.environ` so API keys are present before any tool is
instantiated, even when a tool is imported directly (not via the registry). Resolve the
env file via `app_paths.env_path()` (lazy `from lib import app_paths` — the SAME file the
BYOK panel writes); on ANY failure fall back to the repo-root `.env`
(`Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / ".env"`). Return early if it is missing.
Read it (utf-8, `errors="ignore"`), and per line: strip; skip blanks, `#` comments, and
lines without `=`; split on the first `=`; strip the key; strip whitespace then surrounding
`'`/`"` from the value. Strip an INLINE comment only when the `#` is preceded by whitespace
— `"  #"` (two spaces) or a tab — so a `#` inside a value (e.g. a hex color) survives.
Set the var only when the key is truthy and NOT already in `os.environ` (so a mid-session
key reaches a freshly-spawned subprocess without clobbering the live environment).

## Enums (all `class X(str, Enum)`; values are the lowercased member names unless noted)

- `ToolTier`: CORE, VOICE, ENHANCE, GENERATE, SOURCE, ANALYZE, PUBLISH.
- `ToolStability`: EXPERIMENTAL, BETA, PRODUCTION.
- `ToolStatus`: AVAILABLE, UNAVAILABLE, DEGRADED.
- `ToolRuntime` — where/how a tool executes: LOCAL (on-device, free, no network),
  LOCAL_GPU (`"local_gpu"`, needs GPU VRAM), API (external API, needs key, costs money),
  HYBRID (local OR API, e.g. image_selector).
- `ExecutionMode`: SYNC, ASYNC.
- `Determinism`: DETERMINISTIC, SEEDED, STOCHASTIC.
- `ResumeSupport`: NONE, FROM_START (`"from_start"`), FROM_CHECKPOINT (`"from_checkpoint"`).

## Dataclasses

- `ResourceProfile` — hardware envelope: cpu_cores=1, ram_mb=512, vram_mb=0, disk_mb=100,
  network_required=False.
- `RetryPolicy` — safe retry behavior: max_retries=0, backoff_seconds=1.0,
  retryable_errors=[] (`field(default_factory=list)`).
- `ToolResult` — standard execution result: success (bool, required), data={} and
  artifacts=[] (default_factory), error=None, cost_usd=0.0, duration_seconds=0.0,
  seed: Optional[int]=None, model: Optional[str]=None.

## `BaseTool(ABC)` — class attributes (overridden in subclasses), with these defaults

- Identity: name="", version="0.1.0", tier=CORE, stability=EXPERIMENTAL,
  execution_mode=SYNC, determinism=DETERMINISTIC, runtime=LOCAL.
- Dependencies: dependencies=[] (for API tools add `"env:ENVVAR"` to signal required keys),
  install_instructions="".
- Capabilities: capability="generic", provider="opennolan", capabilities=[], input_schema={},
  output_schema={}, artifact_schema={}, progress_schema: Optional[dict]=None, supports={},
  best_for=[], not_good_for=[], provider_matrix={}.
- Resource & retry: resource_profile=ResourceProfile(), retry_policy=RetryPolicy().
- Resume & idempotency: resume_support=NONE, idempotency_key_fields=[].
- Side effects & fallback: side_effects=[], fallback: Optional[str]=None, fallback_tools=[].
- `agent_skills=[]` — names of installed `.agents/skills/` skills teaching the underlying
  tech; the orchestrator loads these when planning tool usage.
- `user_visible_verification=[]`.
- Optional scoring hints (leave None unless a real measured value exists — `lib/scoring.py`
  uses them directly instead of stability heuristics): quality_score,
  historical_success_rate, latency_p50_seconds, all `Optional[float]=None`.

## `BaseTool` methods

- `get_status() -> ToolStatus`: call `check_dependencies`; AVAILABLE on success,
  UNAVAILABLE on DependencyError.
- `check_dependencies() -> None`: for each dep, dispatch by prefix and raise
  `DependencyError` (message + `install_instructions`) if unsatisfied — `cmd:<name>` →
  missing when `shutil.which(name) is None`; `env:<name>` → missing when
  `os.environ.get(name)` is falsy; `python:<module>` → missing when `__import__(module)`
  raises ImportError. Ignore deps with any other prefix.
- `get_info() -> dict[str, Any]`: full tool contract for registry/discovery. Include every
  identity/capability/resource field, with enums as their `.value`. Notable computed keys:
  `status` = `get_status().value`; `module_path` = `self.__class__.__module__`;
  `usage_location` = `inspect.getfile(self.__class__)`; `resource_profile` expanded to a
  dict of its five fields; `fallback_tools` = `self.fallback_tools or ([self.fallback] if
  self.fallback else [])`; `related_skills` = `agent_skills` (duplicate key). Also emit
  quality_score / historical_success_rate / latency_p50_seconds.
- `estimate_cost(inputs) -> float` = 0.0; `estimate_runtime(inputs) -> float` = 0.0
  (override in paid / long-running tools).
- `idempotency_key(inputs) -> str`: sha256 of `json.dumps({k: inputs.get(k) for k in
  idempotency_key_fields}, sort_keys=True)`, hex, first 16 chars.
- `execute(inputs) -> ToolResult`: `@abstractmethod` — subclasses implement.
- `dry_run(inputs) -> dict`: preflight with no side effects (override for paid/publishing) —
  `{tool: name, estimated_cost_usd, estimated_runtime_seconds, status: get_status().value,
  would_execute: True}`.
- `run_command(cmd, *, timeout=None, cwd=None) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess`: subprocess
  helper. On Windows resolve `cmd[0]` via `shutil.which` (so `.cmd`/`.bat` wrappers like
  npx/npm are found without `shell=True`), otherwise run cmd as given. `subprocess.run` with
  `capture_output=True, text=True, timeout, cwd, check=True`.

## `DependencyError(Exception)` — raised when a tool's dependency is not satisfied.
